# Commercial S9 Git-index mode preflight diagnosis

## Observed

After canonical Control sync, the S9 deployment stopped before service mutation
with `S8_BACKUP_RED GIT_INDEX_MODE_DRIFT` while re-verifying the already green
recovery point.

## Root cause

The server's secure `0027` umask caused Git to replace the Control index with
mode `0640`. The existing bounded index normalizer accepted a newly-created
`0644` index but not the equally non-world-readable `0640` variant.

## Resolution

Add a strictly S9-scoped Control-index normalization before recovery-point
verification. It accepts only the observed `0640` mode and the already-normal
`0660` mode, normalizing `0640` to `0660`. The historical S8 backup artifact and
its hash stay byte-exact. Ownership, regular-file and non-symlink guards remain
unchanged. No repository content, credential, database or service state is
modified by normalization.

## Rollback

Revert this correction commit. S8 remained active and unchanged because the
controller failed before the first service mutation.
